{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "F11RelationCannotBeJoinedToItself",
    "description": "REPRO, EXPECTED TO FAIL. Two `ranges` drawing from the SAME index set make every `join.on` key column unresolvable, so a relation cannot be joined to itself.\n\n    Compile failed: Unsupported feature 'value-equality join over data-derived\n    columns': join key column 'r_priorID' does not resolve to a loop index of\n    this aggregate ({\"b\", \"a\"}): it names neither a range symbol, nor an index\n    set one of those ranges draws from, nor a declared 1-D data column over\n    such an index set (RFC semiring-faq-unified-ir §5.3)\n\nThe message's own last clause is satisfied: `r_priorID` IS a declared 1-D data column over `row_ax`, and `row_ax` IS the index set both ranges draw from. What fails is the resolution STRATEGY -- a key column is matched to a loop symbol by its axis, so two symbols over one axis are ambiguous and neither is chosen. It is a build error rather than a silent zero, which is the right failure mode; it is recorded because the shape it forbids is a common one and the workaround is not free.\n\nWHY MOVES WANTS THIS. Three joins of docs/nonroad-logging-county.md §3 are naturally self-joins: J6 pairs nrstatesurrogate's county row with the STATE row of the same table on the same surrogate; the growth series needs the indicator at the previous year, from the same series; and scrptime's per-age scrappage walk reads the previous age's cumulative percent, from the same age relation.\n\nWORKAROUND, in use in three components: build a SECOND relation over a SECOND index set holding the query side, and join the two. components/geographic_allocation.esm materializes a 4-row (surrogate, FIPS) target relation instead of pairing nrstatesurrogate with itself; components/growth_index.esm keeps its factor rows in `growth_factor_rows` and its indicator rows in `growth_query_rows`, which is why the prior-year lookup is a plain join; components/age_distribution.esm evaluates the scrappage step function TWICE, once at the age's life fraction and once at the previous age's, rather than reading the neighbouring row. Each costs a relation the model does not otherwise need, and the last one costs a second contraction over the 197-point curve.\n\n**Fix shape.** Resolve a key column to the range symbol whose expression body indexes it, falling back to the axis rule only when that is unambiguous; or admit an explicit `[symbol, column]` spelling in the pair so the author can disambiguate. The pair list is already the place where the author says what joins to what.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["finding", "expected-to-fail", "joins", "relational"]
  },

  "index_sets": { "row_ax": { "kind": "interval", "size": 5 } },

  "models": {
    "F11RelationCannotBeJoinedToItself": {
      "tolerance": { "rel": 1e-12 },
      "variables": {
        "r_id": { "type": "unknown", "shape": ["row_ax"], "description": "The relation's key column." },
        "r_priorID": { "type": "unknown", "shape": ["row_ax"], "description": "The key of the row before this one: a shifted copy of r_id, and the whole point of the join." },
        "r_value": { "type": "unknown", "shape": ["row_ax"], "description": "The payload." },
        "r_priorValue": { "type": "unknown", "shape": ["row_ax"], "units": "1", "description": "The previous row's payload, read by joining the relation to itself on the shifted key." }
      },
      "equations": [
        { "lhs": "r_id", "rhs": { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5] } },
        { "lhs": "r_priorID", "rhs": { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4] } },
        { "lhs": "r_value", "rhs": { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": [10, 20, 30, 40, 50] } },
        {
          "lhs": "r_priorValue",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate", "args": [], "semiring": "sum_product", "output_idx": ["a"],
            "ranges": { "a": { "from": "row_ax" }, "b": { "from": "row_ax" } },
            "join": [ { "on": [["r_priorID", "r_id"]] } ],
            "expr": { "op": "index", "args": ["r_value", "b"] }
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "a_relation_can_be_joined_to_itself",
          "description": "INTENDED behaviour. Row 1 has no predecessor and reads the additive identity; every other row reads the value of the row before it. When this goes green, three components in this repo can drop a relation each.",
          "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.0 },
          "assertions": [
            { "variable": "r_priorValue", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0, "coords": { "row_ax": 1 } },
            { "variable": "r_priorValue", "time": 0.0, "expected": 10.0, "coords": { "row_ax": 2 } },
            { "variable": "r_priorValue", "time": 0.0, "expected": 40.0, "coords": { "row_ax": 5 } }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
